From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: msi: an installer's feature tree shows its states, description and size

PuTTY's installer (David's report) showed its feature list without the state
icons, and "FeaturesDlgItemDescription" and "FeaturesDlgItemSize" where the
selected feature's description and size belong. The selection tree's
subclass returned CallWindowProc's LRESULT as an HRESULT: on 64-bit every
tree item handle was cut to 32 bits, so the state icons were never set and
the first feature never selected. The first feature is also selected again
once the dialog is built (the texts subscribe after the tree is made and
missed the event), and the selection's size is published ("This feature
requires 5.79 MB on your hard drive.", in the package's own words when its
UIText has them) -- nothing sent SelectionSize.

Gate: make test-msiseltree.
--- a/dlls/msi/dialog.c
+++ b/dlls/msi/dialog.c
@@ -2383,7 +2383,11 @@
 {
     struct msi_selection_tree_info *info;
     TVHITTESTINFO tvhti;
-    HRESULT r;
+    /* Stained Glass OS: an LRESULT -- as an HRESULT it cut the tree's item
+     * handles to 32 bits on 64-bit, and every feature lost its state icon and
+     * the first one was never selected (its description never shown:
+     * "FeaturesDlgItemDescription" in PuTTY's installer) */
+    LRESULT r;
 
     TRACE("%p %04x %#Ix %#Ix\n", hWnd, msg, wParam, lParam);
 
@@ -2461,6 +2465,15 @@
     /* select the first item */
     SendMessageW( hwnd, TVM_SELECTITEM, TVGN_CARET | TVGN_DROPHILITE, (LPARAM) hfirst );
     info->selected = hfirst;
+
+    /* Stained Glass OS: and once the dialog is built, again: the controls
+     * showing the selection's description and size subscribe after the tree
+     * is made, and missed its event (PuTTY showed "FeaturesDlgItemDescription") */
+    if (!parent && hfirst)
+    {
+        PostMessageW( hwnd, TVM_SELECTITEM, TVGN_CARET, 0 );
+        PostMessageW( hwnd, TVM_SELECTITEM, TVGN_CARET, (LPARAM) hfirst );
+    }
 }
 
 static void seltree_create_imagelist( HWND hwnd )
@@ -2512,6 +2525,8 @@
 
     if (tv->hdr.code != TVN_SELCHANGINGW)
         return ERROR_SUCCESS;
+    if (!tv->itemNew.hItem)
+        return ERROR_SUCCESS;
 
     info->selected = tv->itemNew.hItem;
 
@@ -2533,6 +2548,28 @@
     MSI_RecordSetStringW( rec, 1, MSI_RecordGetString( row, 4 ) );
     msi_event_fire( dialog->package, L"SelectionDescription", rec );
 
